[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.35]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (10,0);
\coordinate (C) at (15.29,6);
\coordinate (D) at (5.29,6);
\coordinate (F) at (10.92,1.04);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,below right,font=\small] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw[dashed] (3,0) -- (3,6) node[midway,left,font=\small] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (3,0.6) -- (3.6,0.6) -- (3.6,0);
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (F) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$x$};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.3cm] {angle = C--F--D};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The parallelogram has a base of $10\text{ cm}$ and a perpendicular height of $6\text{ cm}$. What is the value of $x$, the perpendicular height drawn to the $8\text{ cm}$ side, in centimetres?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.35]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (10,9);
\node[below,font=\small] at (5,0) {$10\text{ cm}$};
\node[left,font=\small] at (0,4.5) {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw (14,0) -- (26,0) node[midway,below,font=\small] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\draw (26,0) -- (19,7.5);
\draw (19,7.5) -- (14,0);
\draw[dashed] (19,0) -- (19,7.5) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$x$};
\draw (19,0.6) -- (19.6,0.6) -- (19.6,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The area of the triangle is half the area of the rectangle. What is the value of $x$, in centimetres?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.32]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (15,14);
\draw (0,14) rectangle (8.4,18);
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (7.5,7) {$A=210\text{ cm}^2$};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (4.2,16) {$A=33.6\text{ cm}^2$};
\node[left,font=\small] at (0,16) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (15,7) {$x$};
\draw[gray,thin] (8.4,18) -- (8.4,20.2);
\draw[gray,thin] (15,14) -- (15,20.2);
\draw[<->] (8.4,19.6) -- (15,19.6) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$6.6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The figure is made from two rectangles and the area of each is shown. What is the value of $x$, in centimetres?
